  "content": {
    "id": "p14-practice-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "",
    "prompt": "Find where the curve is increasing or decreasing.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p14-practice-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$y=-2x^2+8x-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Increasing: $x<2$.\n\nDecreasing: $x>2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y'&=-4x+8\\end{align*}$$\nIncreasing when $y'>0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}-4x+8&>0\\\\-4x&>-8\\\\x&<2\\end{align*}$$\nDecreasing when $y'<0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}-4x+8&<0\\\\-4x&<-8\\\\x&>2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-practice-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=2x^2-x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Increasing: $x>\\frac14$.\n\nDecreasing: $x<\\frac14$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y'&=4x-1\\end{align*}$$\nIncreasing when $y'>0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}4x-1&>0\\\\4x&>1\\\\x&>\\frac14\\end{align*}$$\nDecreasing when $y'<0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}4x-1&<0\\\\4x&<1\\\\x&<\\frac14\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-practice-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$y=x^3-3x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Increasing: $x<-1$ or $x>1$.\n\nDecreasing: $-1<x<1$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y'&=3x^2-3\\\\y'&=3(x-1)(x+1)\\end{align*}$$\nThe derivative is zero at $x=-1$ and $x=1$. Its quadratic graph opens upwards.\n\nIncreasing when $3(x-1)(x+1)>0$, so $x<-1$ or $x>1$.\n\nDecreasing when $3(x-1)(x+1)<0$, so $-1<x<1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-practice-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$y=4x^3-24x^2+36x-8$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Increasing: $x<1$ or $x>3$.\n\nDecreasing: $1<x<3$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y'&=12x^2-48x+36\\\\y'&=12(x^2-4x+3)\\\\y'&=12(x-1)(x-3)\\end{align*}$$\nThe derivative is zero at $x=1$ and $x=3$. Its quadratic graph opens upwards.\n\nIncreasing when $12(x-1)(x-3)>0$, so $x<1$ or $x>3$.\n\nDecreasing when $12(x-1)(x-3)<0$, so $1<x<3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 53
      }
    ]
  },
